<title>INDIA: Indian bullion markets closed for Hindu festival.</title>
<headline>Indian bullion markets closed for Hindu festival.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian bullion markets were closed on Thursday for a local Hindu festival, dealers said.</p>
<p>They reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, gold and silver opened higher and gained further towards the close on the back of recovering world markets, dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;Physical demand for approaching festivals as well as eased pressure of arrivals at the lower level also helped the recovery in the local market,&quot; one dealer said.  </p>
<p>	    WEDNESDAY'S CLOSING (BOMBAY)	  PVS CLOSING</p>
<p>Gold 24 carat     5,130 rupees per 10 gms  (+15)   5,115</p>
<p>Gold 22 carat     4,745			  (+15)   4,730</p>
<p>Silver.999	  6,955 rupees per kg	(+25)   6,930</p>
<p>Silver.916	  6,860			  (+30)   6,830</p>
<p>(Conversion $1=35.64 rupees)</p>
